<title>UK: GECC prices $400 million nine-year bond.</title>
<headline>GECC prices $400 million nine-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond announced</p>
<p>earlier by lead managers Goldman Sachs International and SBC Warburg has been priced.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORP</p>
<p> AMT	  $400 MLN  COUPON     7.00	MATURITY    12.JUN.06</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.807   PAY DATE    12.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    100.132   SPREAD	+22 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) =	   SALE LIMITS US/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.325     SELL CONC  1.675     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.625 PCT U.S. T-NOTE DUE 15.MAY.07 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
